# CHANGELOG.md

`CHANGELOG.md` (Keep a Changelog) lists notable changes to the example applications. It covers this repo only. Compiler, runtime package, docs, AI dev guide, and IDE client changes have their own changelogs.

## When you make a change

- When a change you make is notable to someone running the examples (or, for scripts and tooling, to maintainers), add one line for it under `## [Unreleased]` as part of the same change, before you report the work done. Use the matching group: `### Added`, `### Changed`, `### Deprecated`, `### Removed`, `### Fixed`, `### Security`. Create the group if it is missing.
- Start each line with the example directory it affects (`chirper: …`). Use `All examples: …` for changes across every example.
- Write for someone cloning and running the examples: new or removed examples, changed commands or behavior, and new required versions of Tyhp, PHP, or Composer packages.
- Refreshed `composer.lock` files with no visible effect and README wording fixes may be left out.
- Editing `CHANGELOG.md` is a normal file edit and needs no commit. Re-read the file right before editing, since other agents may be adding entries.

## When the user asks you to commit

- Review the `[Unreleased]` entries against the diff being committed rather than writing them from scratch: add lines for changes that have none, and condense or correct lines the diff no longer matches. Keep entries for other in-progress work.
- Include the CHANGELOG edit in the commit the user asked for. Never commit just to update it.

## When the user asks you to push a release

The examples are not versioned. When pushing to `main` at the user's request, move the `[Unreleased]` entries under `## YYYY-MM-DD` (push date) and leave an empty `## [Unreleased]` above it, as part of the commit being pushed.
